      "content": "SSC / SSC Important Exam Notes"
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "Article 32 is the very soul of the Constitution and the very heart of it.",
      "id": "xfawy5q"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Articles 14 to 18 guarantee the Right to Equality to all Indian citizens.",
        "Article 21 provides Protection of Life and Personal Liberty, which includes the Right to Privacy and Right to Education (Article 21A).",
        "Article 32 grants the Right to Constitutional Remedies, empowering citizens to approach the Supreme Court directly for Fundamental Rights enforcement.",
        "Article 51A details the Fundamental Duties, incorporated by the 42nd Constitutional Amendment Act of 1976.",
        "Article 368 details the power and procedure of Parliament to amend the Constitution."
      ],
      "id": "a7i92m0"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3rivtss",
      "content": "• Article 32 is called the 'Heart and Soul of the Constitution'."
    },
