    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Article 17 (Abolition of Untouchability) is one of the most repeatedly tested constitutional provisions in SSC exams.",
        "Article 110 defines a Money Bill, where the Speaker of Lok Sabha holds final authority regarding its certification.",
        "Article 280 governs the constitution of the Finance Commission by the President of India every five years.",
        "Emergency Provisions are categorized under Articles 352 (National Emergency), 356 (President's Rule), and 360 (Financial Emergency)."
      ],
      "id": "e15lsck"
    },
